# doc.cosm: the parts of the document that are not nodes: how to read it, where the nonprofit came from, what the model already shows, and the
# sources the P nodes cite. The deck and the pack render these; nothing is hand-assembled.

reading:
  draft: "State draft 0"
  date: 2026-10-18
  author: "@comprise-sample"
  mode: "research (public sources only, one working session); mattering is the modeller's reading, confidence 0.5 unless a source is cited"
  perspective: "The firm is Khan Academy, Inc., the nonprofit. Its sibling Schoolhouse World is a second atom; the related organizations abroad and the affiliated schools nonprofits are stubs; partners, funders and the app stores are outsiders named in C."
  note: "A public sample: no person is named, and what could not be confirmed from a current public source is left pending. Facts change; every figure carries its period."

history:
  - {date: 2026-08, event: "New Khanmigo tools with interactive diagrams and teacher-reviewed practice, backed by a Google.org grant and a six-month fellowship", sources: [blog-google-org]}
  - {date: 2026-02, event: "Gemini models announced for the Writing Coach, and a Reading Coach announced for later in 2026", sources: [journal-google-2026]}
  - {date: 2025-10, event: "The districts experience is rebuilt with Khanmigo built into the platform; all district partners from the 2026-27 school year", sources: [blog-districts-2026]}
  - {date: 2024-06, event: "The fiscal year moves from calendar to July-June, with a six-month short return for January to June 2024", sources: [f990-tp2024, f990-2025]}
  - {date: 2024-05, event: "Khanmigo for Teachers becomes free for US teachers with Microsoft's donated infrastructure; New Hampshire offers Khanmigo statewide", sources: [blog-microsoft, blog-new-hampshire]}
  - {date: 2024-01, event: "Stand Together Trust commits $20 million over five years across Khan Academy, Schoolhouse.world and Khan Lab School", sources: [standtogether]}
  - {date: 2023-10, event: "The College Board describes Official Digital SAT Prep on Khan Academy as launched with the digital SAT", sources: [collegeboard-sat]}
  - {date: 2023-03, event: "Khanmigo is announced as a pilot built on GPT-4", sources: [journal-khanmigo-2023]}
  - {date: 2023, event: "The international partner model: independent local entities bring the offer to school systems", sources: [ka-help-partners]}
  - {date: 2019, event: "The district program launches; MAP Accelerator is announced with NWEA", sources: [blog-districts-2026, blog-nwea-2019]}
  - {date: 2018-07, event: "Khan Academy Kids launches as a free app", sources: [edweek-kids-2018]}
  - {date: 2016-08, event: "Duck Duck Moose joins Khan Academy and its early-learning apps become free", sources: [techcrunch-ddm-2016]}
  - {date: 2015, event: "Official SAT practice begins with the College Board", sources: [collegeboard-sat]}
  - {date: 2008-05, event: "The IRS grants 501(c)(3) exemption to the corporation formed in 2007", sources: [pp-ka, f990-2025]}

findings:
  - check: "claims · evidence"
    nodes: [R:claim/reach]
    finding: "Three public counts of registered users differ by period and definition: 180 million-plus on the home page, 227 million on the About page and more than 185 million on the Form 990 at 30 June 2025."
    proposal: "Publish one definition (accounts with a last-active date) and date every count; until then the model keeps all three and a pending question."
  - check: "economics · price-dissonance"
    nodes: [P:offering/districts-partnership, P:offering/kids-for-schools, P:offering/khanmigo-families]
    finding: "The AI subscription has a public price ($4 a month), while the institutional offerings (districts, Learning Paths, Kids for Schools) have none; the return books $22.2 million of program service revenue and does not split it."
    proposal: "Ask the finance and districts roles for the split of earned revenue and a price range for districts; the model leaves both pending."
  - check: "substrate reuse · duplicate"
    nodes: [P:product/khanmigo-ai, S:system/khanmigo-ai]
    finding: "Khanmigo is described as using GPT-4 (pricing pages), Gemini models (2026 tools) and Microsoft's infrastructure and small models, with no single statement of which serves which feature."
    proposal: "Declare one S node per model route and attach each to the features it serves; the engine's pending question names the gap."
  - check: "role coverage · owner-gap"
    nodes: [P:suite/districts, P:offering/learning-paths, P:service/district-implementation]
    finding: "No public page names who runs district partnerships, although district partnerships are sold to institutions at a price."
    proposal: "Name the owning role; the model gives the chief executive the nodes with a pending question until then."
  - check: "capacity · risk"
    nodes: [P:function/fundraising, C:finance/2022, C:finance/2023]
    finding: "Gifts are 77% of revenue in the year to June 2025 and swing between years: $40.0 million in 2022, $84.2 million in 2023, $20.7 million in the six months to June 2024 and $90.4 million in the year to June 2025."
    proposal: "Model the largest gifts and the donor-restricted share by year if the nonprofit's own reports give them; the model carries only what the returns state."

